---
functor: 1
title: angle
---

set heading(numbering: none)

`angle` · fence · angle brackets, a pairing or an average.

# Form

`(a + b).angle` on a group, `x.angle` on a symbol.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `(a + b).angle` | $(a + b).angle$ | fence around the group |
| `(u, v).angle` | $(u, v).angle$ | fence around the group |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | Angle brackets, a pairing or an average. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | A kind can take this fence from a rule: `set abs(fence: angle)`. |
| Construction | Brackets around a group or a symbol. The brackets grow with the content. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- Works on a group, `(a + b).angle`, or on a symbol, `x.angle`. Write `x2` after it to double the fence. Write `left` or `right` after it to keep one side only. A style rule can give a kind its fence: `set mat(fence: angle)`.

# From LaTeX

`\langle u, v \rangle` becomes `(u, v).angle` or `inner(u, v)`.

